{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/init(_:)"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:6Swidux11EntityStoreVyACyxGSayxGcfc","title":"init(_:)","roleHeading":"Initializer","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"init","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"([","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a store pre-populated from an array (e.g. first-load hydration at app launch)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"initialEntities","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Does ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"text":" record changes — the data is already persisted.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first-load"}]},{"type":"text","text":" hydration only. Do not use this initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to “refresh from disk” mid-session by assigning into a live "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(e.g. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.items = EntityStore(fetched)"},{"type":"text","text":" from a CloudKit re-hydrate action)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In-memory state may hold unflushed writes or live UI bindings; wholesale"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replacement silently drops them and surfaces as lost keystrokes. Use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/merge(from:shouldReplace:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for that path — it records no changes and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lets you decide per-ID which side wins. Under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentCloudKitContainer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the gotcha is especially sharp: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".NSPersistentStoreRemoteChange"},{"type":"text","text":" fires for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"local saves too, so a naïve “refresh on remote change” observer feeds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app its own writes."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Entities sharing an ID are collapsed to the first occurrence. A store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cannot represent duplicates — ","type":"text"},{"code":"positions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds one index per ID — and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"admitting them corrupts the index: the map would keep only the last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index while the array kept every copy, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over-reports and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"later delete orphans the earlier copy with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"positions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entry at all,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaving a row that is visible in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/values"},{"text":" but invisible to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/contains(_:)"},{"text":" and the subscript. Persisted rows can legitimately","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"share an ID (CloudKit forbids unique constraints), so this initializer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has to be total rather than trusting its input.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore\/init(_:)"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore/merge(from:shouldReplace:)":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/merge(from:shouldReplace:)","title":"merge(from:shouldReplace:)","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore\/merge(from:shouldreplace:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Merges entities from another store. Entities only present in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are always added; for IDs present in both, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shouldReplace"},{"type":"text","text":" decides"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether the incoming value overwrites the one already in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"merge